WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.745
♫La, la, la, la, la, la, la

00:00:02.745 --> 00:00:05.241
♫La, la, la, la, la, la♫

00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:06.587
- Can you, can you be random?

00:00:06.587 --> 00:00:08.166
Can you, can you be random?

00:00:08.166 --> 00:00:09.420
Can you be random?

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.406
No, seriously, can you be random?

00:00:11.406 --> 00:00:15.480
(light jazz beat)

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.618
I mean, randomness means

00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:18.441
you have no aim, you have no direction,

00:00:18.441 --> 00:00:20.159
there's no rule, there's no method.

00:00:20.159 --> 00:00:22.040
Sounds like a college student, whatever.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.060
But seriously, can you be random?

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.242
I mean, 'cause sometimes you
think you're being random,

00:00:26.242 --> 00:00:29.186
when in reality there's actually a pattern

00:00:29.186 --> 00:00:31.025
that you don't realize is going on.

00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:32.059
Let me show you.

00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:33.661
I have six boxes.

00:00:33.661 --> 00:00:36.041
And in this game inspired
by Richard Weisman,

00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:38.339
we're gonna start on the green box,

00:00:38.339 --> 00:00:39.825
so put your finger there.

00:00:39.825 --> 00:00:41.184
When I say move,

00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:44.237
you can go right,

00:00:44.237 --> 00:00:45.688
you can go down,

00:00:45.688 --> 00:00:46.767
you can go up,

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:47.557
and you can go left.

00:00:47.557 --> 00:00:49.345
You just can't go diagonal.

00:00:49.345 --> 00:00:52.619
And no matter how random
you think you're being,

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.419
you're always gonna end up
back on the pink square.

00:00:55.419 --> 00:00:57.023
Don't believe me?

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.386
Let's test this out.

00:00:58.386 --> 00:00:59.628
Alright, ready?

00:00:59.628 --> 00:01:01.065
Move one.

00:01:01.065 --> 00:01:04.120
So you're either here now, or you're here.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.831
So we can get rid of that guy right there.

00:01:08.416 --> 00:01:09.742
Are you ready for the rest?

00:01:09.742 --> 00:01:10.721
And move.

00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:11.591
Move.

00:01:11.907 --> 00:01:12.752
Move.

00:01:13.176 --> 00:01:13.774
Move.

00:01:14.244 --> 00:01:14.866
Move.

00:01:15.219 --> 00:01:15.852
Move.

00:01:16.182 --> 00:01:16.804
Move.

00:01:16.996 --> 00:01:18.103
And move.

00:01:18.103 --> 00:01:18.657
Cool.

00:01:18.657 --> 00:01:19.879
We can get rid of that guy.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.389
Round two.

00:01:21.389 --> 00:01:22.938
And move.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:23.739
Move.

00:01:23.943 --> 00:01:24.657
Move.

00:01:24.941 --> 00:01:25.690
Move.

00:01:26.021 --> 00:01:26.631
Move.

00:01:27.482 --> 00:01:28.917
That guy's gone, huh?

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:30.531
Move.

00:01:30.768 --> 00:01:31.436
Move.

00:01:31.686 --> 00:01:32.552
Move.

00:01:32.627 --> 00:01:33.558
Move.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.711
That guy, right?

00:01:35.711 --> 00:01:36.622
Gone.

00:01:37.371 --> 00:01:39.426
Now just move one more time.

00:01:39.437 --> 00:01:40.528
Poof.

00:01:41.538 --> 00:01:42.699
Pink square.

00:01:42.699 --> 00:01:44.138
You're touching the
pink square, aren't ya?

00:01:44.138 --> 00:01:45.137
You are.

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:46.460
I told you.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:47.737
You were gonna touch the pink square.

00:01:47.737 --> 00:01:49.154
I told you this at the beginning.

00:01:49.154 --> 00:01:50.675
We had this conversation.

00:01:50.675 --> 00:01:51.719
Sorry.

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:53.298
Am I a mind reader?

00:01:53.298 --> 00:01:55.110
Eh, not so much.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.444
I just gave you the illusion of choice,

00:01:57.444 --> 00:02:00.195
but in reality, I limited your options

00:02:00.195 --> 00:02:01.991
so you'd pick what I wanted.

00:02:01.991 --> 00:02:03.677
Let me show you what I mean.

00:02:03.677 --> 00:02:05.489
Okay, let's go back to the
beginning of the trick,

00:02:05.489 --> 00:02:06.975
which is actually a math problem.

00:02:06.975 --> 00:02:08.356
So we started out here,

00:02:08.356 --> 00:02:10.817
and your first move was
either here or here,

00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:13.544
and then I asked you to move eight times.

00:02:13.544 --> 00:02:16.157
But from either this space or this space,

00:02:16.157 --> 00:02:18.108
it's actually impossible
for you to move eight times

00:02:18.108 --> 00:02:20.497
and get to this space.

00:02:20.497 --> 00:02:21.545
Don't believe me?

00:02:21.545 --> 00:02:23.023
Try it yourself.

00:02:23.023 --> 00:02:25.619
In fact, four moves won't get you there,

00:02:25.619 --> 00:02:27.465
and an even larger number like 16,

00:02:27.465 --> 00:02:29.067
that won't get you there either.

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.715
Wait a minute.

00:02:30.715 --> 00:02:32.643
What does this mean about life?

00:02:32.643 --> 00:02:33.584
What the heck, man?

00:02:33.584 --> 00:02:34.861
I'm gonna have a crisis now.

00:02:34.861 --> 00:02:36.887
What does this mean?

00:02:36.887 --> 00:02:39.841
Seriously, I wonder how much
of life is actually like this.

00:02:39.841 --> 00:02:41.164
I mean, I think I'm being random,

00:02:41.164 --> 00:02:42.418
I think I'm being unpredictable,

00:02:42.418 --> 00:02:44.933
and really I'm just following a pattern.

00:02:52.086 --> 00:02:53.546
Seriously?

